    "content": "Lauren Betts's parents are Andy and Michelle Betts, both accomplished former athletes who met at Long Beach State. Her father, Andy, played professional basketball in Europe for 14 years after being drafted by the Charlotte Hornets, while her mother, Michelle, was a standout volleyball player who won a national championship in 1993. Key details about Lauren Betts's parents: Andy Betts (Father): A 7-foot-1 center who played for the Great Britain/England national team and top European clubs, including Real Madrid. Michelle Betts (Mother): Played volleyball at Long Beach State and later worked as an academic advisor and mentor. Family Background: Lauren was born in Spain while her father played there, and the family lived in various European countries before settling in Colorado. Siblings: Lauren has three siblings: sister Sienna (also on the UCLA basketball team), and brothers Dylan and Ashton. Family Status: Andy and Michelle are divorced but maintained shared custody of their children. The couple, often described as fostering a supportive athletic environment, raised their children to pursue their own interests.",
